.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAG-DELETE-ROUTE 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eag-delete-route \- remove a gateway route
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eag delete-route
.BR \-\-route\-id | \-r
.I ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a route. Its path stops being served within a few seconds and
callers get 404 from then on.
.PP
Nothing else is touched: the application behind it keeps running, and
any other route pointing at the same application keeps working. Deleting
a route is a change to what euclid publishes, not to what it runs.
.PP
To take a path out of service without losing how it was configured, use
.B "update-route \-\-active false"
instead \- see
.BR euclid-cli-eag-update-route (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-route\-id " " \fIID\fR
Route to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The route is gone, including when it was already not there.
.TP
.B 1
Missing arguments, no administrator session, or the server rejected the
request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eag delete-route --route-id datenlieferanten
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eag (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eag-update-route (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eag-list-routes (1)
